1,0$
1,2 $ Monomitic hyphal system in subiculum or context
1,4 $ Dimitic hyphal system in subiculum
2,0 $ Skeletocystidia absent $ Steccherinum adustum (Schwein.) Banker 
2,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, pileate, stipitate or sessile, pileal surface clay-buff to yellowish brown, zonate; spines up to 2mm long, 4-8 per mm. Hyphal system monomitic in context, dimitic in trama, tissues change brown in KOH. Skeletocystidia and cystidia absent. Basidiospores cylindrical, (2.8-)3-3.6(-3.8)×1.2-1.7(-1.8) µm, L=3.18 µm, W=1.39 µm, Q=2.29 (n=30/1).
2,3 $ Skeletocystidia present
3,0 $ Aculei 1.5mm long $ S. aggregatum Hjortstam & Spooner 
3,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate, adnate, pale mouse-gray to light vinaceous gray; spines up to 1.5mm long, 3-5 per mm. Hyphal system monomitic in subiculum, dimitic in trama, skeletal hyphae rare. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia present, clavate to cylindrical. Basidiospores broadly ellipsoid, (3.4-)3.7-4.3(-4.5)×(2.6-)2.7-3.1(-3.3) µm, L=3.88 µm, W=2.89 µm, Q=1.34 (n=31/1).
3,0 $ Aculei 0.5mm long $ S. queletii (Bourdot & Galzin) Hallenb. & Hjortstam 
3,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate, adnate, gray-buff to pale ochraceous; aculei up to 0.5mm long, 4-6 per mm. Hyphal system monomitic in subiculum, dimitic in trama. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate to subulate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, (4.6-)4.7-5.3(-5.9)×3-3.5(-3.7) µm, L=5.05 µm, W=3.25 µm, Q=1.55 (n=30/1).
4,5 $ Subiculum or context duplex
4,6 $ Subiculum or context homogeneous
5,0 $ Basidiospores subglobose $ S. subglobosum 
5,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, effused-reflexed or pileate, pileal surface grayish buff to light vinaceous gray, zonate; spines up to 2mm long, 3-5 per mm. Context duplex, lower layer white to cream, upper layer gray  to dark gray. Hyphal pegs present. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia present, clavate to cylindrical. Basidiospores subglobose, 3.9-4.6(-4.7)×3.3-3.9(-4) µm, L=4.17 µm, W=3.62 µm, Q=1.14-1.17 (n=90/3).
5,0 $ Basidiospores ellipsoid $ S. ochraceum 
5,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate, effused-reflexed or pileate, pileal surface ochraceous to salmon-colored, zonate; spines up to 2mm long, 4-6 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, 3-3.4(-3.6)×(1.9-)2-2.3(-2.6) µm, L=3.24 µm, W=2.18 µm, Q=1.48 (n=30/1).
6,7 $ Skeletocystidia mostly subulate, apex acute
6,9 $ Skeletocystidia mostly clavate, apex blunt
7,0 $ Basidiospores > 5 µm long $ S. oreophilum
7,0 ,n$  Frb. annual, effuse-reflexed to pileate, small-sized, pileal surface glabrous, cream or white, azonate; spines up to 2mm long, 2-4 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, subulate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores narrowly ellipsoid, (5.5-)5.6-5.9(-6)×3-3.2(-3.3) µm, L=5.78 µm, W=3.08 µm, Q=1.88 (n=30/1).
7,8 $ Basidiospores < 5 µm long
8,0 $ Fruitbody reddish to brick-colored $ S. laeticolor
 8,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed, reddish-orange to brick-colored; aculei 0.5-1.5mm long, 3-5 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, subulate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores narrowly ellipsoid to subcylindrical, (2.7-)2.8-3.5(-3.6)×1.8-2(-2.2) µm, L=3.21 µm, W=1.97 µm, Q=1.63 (n=30/1).
8,0 $ Fruitbody white to pinkish buff $ S. subulatum 
8,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed, grayish buff to clay pink, azonate; aculei up to 1mm long, 1-3 per mm when young, 3-6 per mm when old. Skeletocystidia abundant, subulate. Cystidia present, clavate. Basidiospores broadly ellipsoid, (3.7-)3.8-5(-5.1)×(2-)2.3-3 µm, L=4.12 µm, W=2.75 µm, Q=1.46-1.52 (n=90/3).
9,10 $ Fruitbody effused, rarely effused-reflexed
9,11 $ Fruitbody effused-reflexed to pileate
10,0 $ Fruitbody usually form broom-like rhizomorphs $ S. fimbriatum 
10,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate, adnate, pale violaceous or grey-reddish, margin filamentous to rhizomorphs; aculei less than 0.5mm long, 5-7 per mm, tissues change brown in KOH. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, (3-)3.1-3.7(-4)× (2-)2.1-2.4(-2.5) µm, L=3.34 µm, W=2.22 µm, Q=1.5 (n=30/1).
10,0 $ Fruitbody never form broom-like rhizomorphs $ S. mukhinii Kotir. & Y. C. Dai 
10,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, strictly resupinate, adnate, cream when fresh, becoming light gray-buff when dry; spines soft, up to 2mm long, 4-6 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, (2.7-)2.8-3.2(-3.3)×1.7-2(-2.1) µm, L=3.03 µm, W=1.79 µm, Q=1.69 (n=30/1).
11,12 $ Basidiospores < 4 µm long
11,13 $ Basidiospores > 4 µm long
12,0 $ Aculei 3-4mm, pilei margin sharp $ S. murashkinskyi 
12,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed, reflexed part ochraceous, zonate; spines soft, up to 4mm long, 3-4 per mm, Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, (3-)3.1-3.6(-3.8)×1.7-1.9(-2) µm, L=3.31 µm, W=1.83 µm, Q=1.81 (n=30/1).
12,0 $ Aculei up to 2mm, pilei margin blunt $ S. rawakense (Pers.) Banker 
12,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed or pileate, pileal surface yellowish brown, zonate reddish-brown; spines up to 2mm long, 4-5 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, surface smooth or encrusted, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores ellipsoid, (2.7-)2.8-3.2(-3.3)×1.7-2(-2.1) µm, L=2.97 µm, W=1.84 µm, Q=1.61 (n=30/1).
13,0 $ Basidiospores subglobose $ S. hydneum Rick ex Maas Geest 
13,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, effused-reflexed, cinnamon-buff to pinkish buff; spines up to 3mm long, 3-6 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores subglobose, with a big guttule, 4.2-5(-5.3)×(3.5-)3.6-4.1(-4.4) µm, L=4.54 µm, W=3.84 µm, Q=1.18 (n=30/1).
13,14 $ Basidiospores ellipsoid
14,0 $ Aculei 3mm $ S. robustius 
14,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed, reddish-orange when fresh, becoming pinkish-buff or dirty-yellow when dry; spines up to 3mm long, 5-7 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, subclavate to clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores broadly ellipsoid, (4.1-)4.3-4.7(-4.8)×(2.2-)2.3-2.7 µm, L=4.47 µm, W=2.53 µm, Q=1.77 (n=30/1).
14,0 $ Aculei 0.5mm $ S. ciliolatum 
14,0 ,n$ Frb. annual, resupinate, adnate, white to pale ochraceous; aculei up to 0.6mm long, 6-8 per mm. Skeletocystidia abundant, clavate. Cystidia absent. Basidiospores narrowly ellipsoid to cylindrical, (3.9-)4.2-4.7(-4.9)×(1.9-)2.1-2.4 µm, L=4.48 µm, W=2.24

